Description: Sanity check for linux-firmware files
Author: Erico Nunes <ernunes@redhat.com>

linux-firmware sanity Introduction
==================================

This test checks that files in the linux-firmware RHEL package are the
same ones provided by the linux-firmware upstream repository.
We check that the files are the same through the use of checksums.
In case a checksum does not match, we also provide the expected and
found file(1) output to help in debugging the reason for why the file is
different.
This is just a sanity check and it is performed due to past occurences
of firmware files being shipped incorrectly.
